#!/usr/bin/env xetal
## Hello library: a program using two libraries of its own,
## userlibs/Hello.xtl and userlibs/Greetings.xtl. Run it from the
## repository's root with "xetal run demos/hello-library.xtl" (or
## "./demos/hello-library.xtl"); it prints a greeting and two personal
## greetings. Read the imports for how u_se< finds a library: "Hello" is
## Hello.xtl beside this file, then in userlibs/, then on XETAL_PATH,
## then among the standard libraries; the string on its left is the
## prefix the library's l: names get here.

### The imports

"hi:" u_se< "Hello"
"g:" u_se< "Greetings"

### Calling the libraries

# h_ello is niladic: it takes Unit (@), the value that stands for
# nothing, and gives the greeting.
hi:h_ello @

# g_reet is monadic: this program supplies the greeting.
g:g_reet "hi"
g:g_reet "welcome to"
